score["red"] += 3
score["blue"] += 2
score["red"] -= 1
score["green"] = score["blue"] * 2
del score["blue"]
```
labels: score["red"] | score["green"] | len(score) | "blue" in score
answer: 2 | 4 | 2 | False
wrong[2 | 4 | 3 | False]: `del score["blue"]` removes the blue pair, so 2 pairs are left: red and green.
wrong[2 | 4 | 2 | True]: After `del`, "blue" isn't a key anymore, so `in` gives False.
wrong[3 | 4 | 2 | False]: red goes up by 3 and then down by 1: 0 + 3 - 1 = 2.
